  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a poster, I want to insert a GIF from a search, as in the legacy app, so that this function is not lost.\n\n### Scope\n\nSearch and trending sheet over LOT-098 (#190), first-use notice N1 before the first request (host and operator named, search terms are the only data sent), inserts `[img]<gif URL>[/img]` as legacy; GIF previews loaded through the cookie-less client.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: medium · post-MVP\n- Implements: legacy parity (no FEAT)\n- Absorbs: Phase 4 backlog 'Giphy (E-10)'; LOT-071 T5 (kept) + notice N1\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): `AnswerView.swift:2305-2335`\n- Spec: `docs/lots/LOT-155-*.md`\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-098 (#190, done)\n- LOT-084 (#176, done)\n- LOT-071 (#95, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- CAP-N7 (#175): Giphy REST API: one `search` and one `trending` response (rating R), recorded on the Mac with the key stripped from URLs and bodies\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] No request before N1; feature hidden when no key is configured.\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
